description.p:
We give 27 examples of achieving the invention referring to figures 1...30 representing: 

 figure 1: the general design of principle containing the proposed solution, according to the first accomplishing example; figure 2: the design for the version with checking valves located only in die inner cylinder according to the second accomplishing example; figure 3: the design for the version widi two rod guidings, according to die third accomplishing example; figure 4: the design of principle for the version with the rod guiding and sealing located in the superior block according to the fourth accomplishing example; figure 5: the design for the version widi the piston located to die centre of the rod, according to the fifth accomplishing example; figure 6: the design for the version with the valves filled through siphoning, according to the sixth accomplishing example; figure 7: die design for the version widi lateral pressurized compensation, according to the seventh accomplishing example; figure 8: the design for the version with external compensation, for working in any position, according to the eighth accomplishing example; figure 9: the design for the version with lateral compensation, for working in semihorizontal position, according to the ninth accomplishing example; figure 10: longitudinal section for the version with compensation tl rough die pressurized bladder, according to the tenth accomplishing example; figure 11 : cross section for the version with compensation tlirough the pressurized bladder, according to the tenth accomplishing example; figure 12: the design for die version with compensation through exterior pleated tube , according to the eleventh accomplishing example; figure 13: the design for die version with compensation through compensation chamber placed in the lower part of the tank cylinder, with the liquid separated from d e gas tlirough a floating piston-versi on 1, according to the twelfth accomplishing example; figure 14: the design for the version widi compensation through compensation chamber placed in the lower part of d e tank cylinder with the liquid separated from d e gas through a floating piston - version 2, according to die d irteenth accomplishing example; figure 15: the design for the version with compensation drrougli the compensation chamber located in the lower pail of the tank cylinder widi die liquid separated from the gas through floating piston - version 3, according to the fourteentii accomplishing example; figure 16: die design for the simple version using slots as controlling valves, according to the fifteenth accomplishing example; figure 17: the design for the version with a poros inner cylinder, according to die sixteenth accomplishing example; 

